  "prefLabel": "Ins 1101.02 Scope",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 1101.02 Scope. This chapter shall apply to all insurers, their producers, and any other person engaged in the business of insurance in this state who requires an individual applying for insurance or for any increased or additional insurance benefits to be tested for an antibody or antigen to a human immunodeficiency virus.\n\nSource. #4583, eff 1-24-89; ss by #5650, eff 7-1-93; ss by #6953, eff 3-1-99, ss by #8826, eff 3-1-07, EXPIRED: 3-1-15\n\nNew. #10866, eff 7-1-15; ss by #14512, eff 2-7-26, EXPIRES: 2-7-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins1100.html"
